          "prompt": "From: Buddy Williams <buddy.williams@insurity.com>\nSubject: State sync stuck in \"changed on multiple nodes\" conflict loop �� dashboard counts non-authoritative for 1h+\n\nBody:\nSummary\r\n\r\n  On my node (default / BO2LNXNEVO04 (QA), Refine 4.2.0, daemon on port 8082), state sync has been failing continuously since 2026-08-15T16:34:44Z. Every attempt (roughly\r\n  every minute) returns the same Conflict(\"Refine state changed on multiple nodes: ��\") error and the health record is not resetting. As a result the web dashboard shows the\r\n  banner:\r\n\r\n  �� State sync has failed since 2026-08-15T16:34:44Z. All-node counts are local and non-authoritative until synchronization recovers.\r\n\r\n  ��and the \"All\" tab counts (Backlog 0 / To do 83 / Plan 2 / Implement 5 / Quality 0 / Governance 0 / Review 34 / Done 788 / Failed 5 / Cancelled 3) are just this node's\r\n  local projection.\r\n\r\n  Impact\r\n\r\n  - Fleet-wide roll-up on the Dashboard is not authoritative �� it's the last known snapshot plus this node's local delta.\r\n  - This node's outbound state changes are not being published to origin/refine/state, so the other nodes can't see my work either.\r\n  - Reconciliation isn't self-healing; it's been failing for ~1h 45m with no forward progress.\r\n\r\n  Environment\r\n\r\n  - Refine version: 4.2.0, api_contract_version: 2, launch mode binary\r\n  - Daemon: port 8082, daemon_healthy: true, worker_state: idle, web_available: true, no degraded_integrations\r\n  - Active node: default �� BO2LNXNEVO04 (QA), target root /insurity/ProSuite, agent CLI claude\r\n  - Fleet (5 registered, all enabled): default, bo2lnxnevo03-buddy, bo2lnxnevo02-ethan, BO2LNXIPSAPP01, instance_jason\r\n  - Git remote configured, refine/state branch exists, state_sync_debounce_seconds=5, state_sync_stale_threshold_seconds=900\r\n\r\n  Timeline (all UTC)\r\n\r\n  �������������������������������������������������������������������Щ�����������������������������